course: dictionary
lesson: 7679
title: Finding the right meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the sentence around the word and look for clues. The word prosper has two main meanings: to do well and succeed, and to grow strongly and healthily.
explain: In the Bible, Proverbs 28:13 says, «Whoever conceals their sins does not prosper, but the one who confesses and renounces them finds mercy.» Here prosper means doing well in life. The sentence sets it against finding mercy, so the clues point to doing well in a good way.
explain: In a story, «The village prospered after the bridge was built» tells you the village did better and grew richer. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «The village did well after the bridge was built.» It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Prosper is a verb. Its other forms are prospers, prospered and prospering.
fact: «Prosper» means to be successful, especially to grow rich or do well over time.
fact: «Prosper» can also mean to grow strongly and be healthy, like plants or animals.
fact: Towns can prosper from trade, and farms can prosper with good harvests.
fact: In Proverbs 28:13, «conceals» means hides, and «renounces» means gives up.
exercise: «The village prospered after the bridge was built.» What does prospered mean here? | Fell down into the river | Was closed off from everyone | Was painted bright blue | *Did well and grew richer
exercise: Which meaning fits a farm with a good harvest? | *Grew strongly and healthily | Was covered in snow | Was sold for less money | Became very small and quiet
exercise: Find and copy one word from the Proverbs sentence that means to hide. | renounces | confesses | mercy | *conceals
test: «May you prosper.» In this blessing, prosper means: | To be very tired | *To do well and be successful | To shout loudly | To sleep soundly
test: Which word shows that something prospered in the past? | prosper | prospering | *prospered | prospers
exam: Which meaning of prosper fits best in «The town prospered from trade»? | To hide from visitors | To shout about the trade | To be cold and grey | *To grow rich and do well over time
